speechtext:
Madam Speaker, to the honourable House of Commons I have a petition from citizens of the City of Saskatoon. It relates to the situation surrounding Nicaragua. The petition reads:
Wherefore the undersigned, your Petitioners, humbly pray and call upon Parliament to call on the United States Government to desist from any actions which violate the principles of self-determination of peoples and the nonintervention of states, as defined by the United Nations;
And further to call on the Canadian Government to pursue seriously a policy which promotes peace and non-intervention in Nicaragua, a policy which condemns American intervention in Nicaragua, and which is committed not to force, but to negotiation.
